---
/**
 * t61 · Long Carrier
 *
 * Crisper corners and a tail carried a row further down, so the mark points
 * at whoever is speaking. The one in the set with any urgency in it.
 *
 * The tail is the lower-left corner rather than an addition to it: the left
 * edge runs straight past the bottom edge and rakes back up to it over 4
 * rows, taper 8-6-4-2. Because that corner is never rounded the bottom edge
 * stays 24 pixels unbroken, and that edge is what still reads as a message
 * at 16px, where the tail itself is barely a pixel and a half.
 *
 * The strongest band offset in the set — two whole rings, so the deep field
 * comes almost to the keyline on the right shoulder while the left one keeps
 * a full meniscus. Radius 6 gives more contour per corner for that to bend
 * around, which is the only reason it can carry that much without going
 * flat.
 *
 * 7 tones peel inward as contour rings, one step per ring, so every band
 * bends around the corners and around the tail — Hozz's meniscus rather than
 * a rectangle dropped inside an outline. The direction is Mozz's, but spent
 * on where the bands sit instead of on extra tones: a pixel's effective
 * depth is pushed inward by up to 2.0 rings on the side facing away from the
 * light, so the meniscus is wide on the lit shoulder and the deep field
 * rises nearly to the keyline on the far one. The keyline carries it too —
 * two key tones, the lit part of the rim taking the lighter.
 *
 * Spending the direction that way is what keeps the middle calm. The field
 * is one flat tone, 189 pixels of it, and no two touching pixels anywhere in
 * the mark are more than one tone apart.
 *
 * The face is supplied and untouched — facePathsAt at md with the compact
 * smile and the family gap of 2, which is exactly 8×8 — centred on the body
 * with the tail ignored: 8 rows of air above and 8 below, measured. Nothing
 * is cleared for it; white on the field is 8.6:1.
 *
 * 10 tones.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

